A merge that correctly leaves its reporting artifact live can never discharge its commitment.

Causal chain:
1. internal/app/landing.go:88 sets state "no_receipt" for an empty input.MergeHead. The label describes a missing supplied head, not necessarily an absent receipt.
2. internal/app/worktree_landing.go:104 fills MergeHead only when the projected commitment has LandingReceipt.
3. LandingReceipt's write in internal/workroom/fold.go:3760 is fed by mergedArtifacts().
4. mergedArtifacts() at fold.go:3894 accepts an approved artifact only if its ID is in receipt.mergePlan.
5. validateMergeReceiptNow at fold.go:1665-1681 builds that plan exclusively from merge_retirements.

Thus discharge is keyed on retirement, although succession discipline may correctly leave the reporting artifact live and classify it in merge_left_live as carried, verified: true.

